I've enjoyed the first game in the series, but in my opinion the second game has couple of disadvantages:
- The same contol as in the first game. No improvements at all which is not ok for sequel;
- Worse location designs. Sometimes you are running back and forward across the same 3-4 rooms searching for keys and opening the doors. At some point you find yourself remembering "whether there was one more door I've missed";
- A lot of shooting. Mercenaries everywhere (even underwater on the sank ship);
- Enemies appear out of nowhere, often behind your back;
- Steam-only issue: no official support for Golden Mask addon;

