Another Supergiant games with mindblowing quality
If a programmer could have a beautiful, artsy, love-wet dream of their work, it would be
Like Bastion, Transistor have its share of unique style
Its art, {
I guess are hand painted like in Bastion, but not the same kind with Bastion's art, it really is the Transistor's art by itself. Definitely captures the feel of futuristic and 'utopia'-ish of the Transistor's city.
}
Its music, {
superbly composed, and have the ambience and notes that its integrated through the story. Also the fact, the protagonist can *hum* (cos her voice are taken, more explanation ingame) along with the music in-game! Its also the telling the Transistor story mood, other than the narrator.
}
Its voicecast, {
narrator, some character ingame, have some sublimely way of speaking that it mesmerize the player (well me, at least) into want to hearing them more. Really helps, as this game story are mostly told by third person.
}
Its combat (and also gameplay), {
vastly different with Bastion. We can fuse 1-2 combat skills (called Function), into a main skills and have all the effect with stacking/multiplying/adding combat characteristic of the main combat skills. And with more than 20 combat skills, you'll have a lot of time mixing and thinking up the best and also curious how it will render out in-game. Same with Bastion, there's also passive booster (only it also use your combat skill for the booster), and limiter to make your game more challenging to gain more exp.
}
The story, {
with Supergiant Games, are always unique and weirdly written. So weird, it's good because you'll hardly see other game like it with good story. There are many interpretation of the story (and of course the ending, cos that's what Transistor in the end matters, in the ending) floating around in the internet, so much I feel that telling my own interpretation is fairly useless.
Some point in the Transistor, the world are made like a systematic program code would look like if it's have a worldy appereance. Hardly any explanation that if its real, or a virtual made up (which a lot of interpretation in the internet trying to solve). Come up with your interpretation and see if it's interesting enough to be made a movie or novel :)
}
Whether you buy this game, got it free, or frugally purchase it with crazy discount rate,
do yourself, for the gaming world, and also the developer, a favor
play the game
finish the story
and recurse through it (for 100% achievment lol )
Prepare yourself for another beautiful journey of Supergiant's.
END()

